# Line endings are declared here rather than left to each clone's
# core.autocrlf. Everything in the repo is already LF; without this file that
# holds only by luck of the contributor's Git config, and a Windows clone with
# autocrlf=false would commit CRLF into make_icons.sh — whose shebang then
# reads as the interpreter "/bin/sh\r" and fails on macOS.
* text=auto

# Wherever it is checked out, a shell script needs LF: see above.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The PowerShell counterpart is Windows-only by definition, and 5.1 is the
# edition least forgiving about LF-only source.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Art is bytes; never let a filter near it.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
